# Inert PMO native-denial provenance, source/pure only

Finance927ed57 unchanged. No native helpers, SQL, fixtures, database, routes, held source or runtime files executed/changed. This is not complete visibility/source/owner orchestration.

One private operation is charged under existing100 processing cap and binds exact registered candidate, actor/PK/keys/default/raw connection and immutable Template/Version/document/binding/report pins. Version materialization happens BEFORE the fixed native binding_access try. Only native PermissionDenied is eligible; ValidationError and engineering/context/codec/SQL errors stay fatal. Normal return also checks clean operation context, including swallowed poison/signal.

The early report.read gate stays before manifest transfer. It alone catches PermissionDenied from the actual require call and registers a private exact _ReportDenied signal, not a PD/VE subtype. guarded bypasses poisoning ONLY for that exact object, exact active native_running operation and clean context. Copied/unregistered signals and all other prepared PD remain fatal. The read boundary consumes the signal once and records native-denial provenance. Normal-success final rechecks are outside this native-denial region and cannot create hidden outcomes. No exception text is retained.

Denial completion never calls binding_for, transfers BYTEA, decodes new bodies or discovers new history. It rechecks registered/scalar Version identity, then SELECT1 with closed binding/Template/Version/document/report/source_mode predicates and manifest stamp only if attained. Only fully completed operation-owned cells get scalar metadata rechecks with their exact expected immutable metadata; each such query spends BOTH scalar permit and global cell-work debit. Own started PMOTicket object identities are registered; any incomplete/reserved/mismatched ticket fails. Touched-cell dedup ORs history mode so later selected access cannot discard an earlier cutoff. Shared cells must still be validated with identical metadata.

Completed cell validation remains evidence of bytes, NOT permission or report visibility. Charges and original tickets remain; denial does not relabel bytes authorized, refund or reset anything. Later fresh operations retain normal fresh query/transfer/decode/gate work. Denied reader cannot resume; a new reader spends new processing. Success may begin another fresh operation subject to caps. Existing global/local100cells/1MiB/cellattempt/scalar limits unchanged.

The terminal repr-suppressed outcome is exact-object registered in the exact operation record, binds context/worklist/row and fixed native/report provenance, and can be privately consumed once. Copied outcomes/operation tickets, context mismatch or old outcome through a new reader poison both original and current entries. Consumption returns no visibility value. There is no blanket conversion of native classes around prepared work and no PMO ValidationError conversion.

24 new pure definitions exercise fixed native/report denial and normal success, copied/unregistered/swallowed signals, prepared same-class errors, VE, pre-native materialization and post-native success failures, completed/pending cells, stronger history-context retention, scalar/metadata guard misses, retained bytes, one-use and copied outcomes, fresh-reader/old-outcome poisoning, operation100/101 and existing attempt limits. Native functions are stand-ins; scalar SQL results are modeled. Actual SQL compilation/evaluation, native grant/default-prepared equivalence, own-write/RR concurrency and DB rollback remain UNRUN. Existing Finance source and tests stay unchanged.
